-- Gives `message_log` the four columns the code reads and writes.
--
-- Generated by hand and reviewed by hand, like the other migrations in this
-- directory.
--
-- ## What this closes
--
-- Production's `message_log` predates `0004_chubby_crystal.sql`. It was created
-- with another shape and `0004`'s `CREATE TABLE` never applied over it. Every
-- column the code reads and writes beyond the shared ones — `direction`,
-- `provider_message_id`, `content`, `metadata` — was missing, so the first
-- WhatsApp send, push delivery or campaign in production would fail on its
-- insert, and the history and deliveries routes would fail on their select.
--
-- The drift gate could not see it: it checks that named objects exist, and
-- `0004`'s evidence named the table and its indexes, never its columns. The
-- evidence registered for this migration names the columns.
--
-- Found on 2026-10-20 by comparing every table of `packages/db/src/schema.ts`
-- against production: `message_log` was the only one of 26 that differed.
--
-- ## Why `direction` is NOT NULL with no default
--
-- That is the column as the schema declares it, and every insert in the code
-- sets it. On an empty table the constraint costs nothing; on a table that
-- holds rows this statement fails, and that failure is wanted — rows written
-- in another shape need a person to decide their direction.
--
-- ## What this migration deliberately leaves as it is
--
-- Production still differs from the schema in ways that break nothing, and
-- that the drift gate could not verify if this migration changed them (it
-- refuses `ALTER COLUMN` and `DROP` as unverifiable evidence):
--
-- - `payload` and `error` exist and the schema does not declare them. Nullable,
--   empty, and read or written by no code.
-- - `customer_id` is nullable; the schema says NOT NULL. Every insert sets it.
-- - `channel` has no default and `status` defaults to `'pending'`; the schema
--   says `'whatsapp'` and `'queued'`. Every insert sets both.
-- - `created_at` is `timestamp` without a time zone; the schema says
--   `timestamptz`. It is filled by `now()`, and the database and the workers
--   both run in UTC, so the stored instant is the same.
--
-- Aligning those is a separate change, and it needs the gate to learn how to
-- verify a type, a default and an absent column first.
--
-- ## Not applied here
--
-- `drizzle-kit migrate` is not how a migration is applied in this repository.
-- A person applies this by hand, after review. This file is left on disk, unrun.
ALTER TABLE "message_log" ADD COLUMN "direction" text NOT NULL;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "message_log" ADD COLUMN "provider_message_id" text;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "message_log" ADD COLUMN "content" jsonb DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb;--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "message_log" ADD COLUMN "metadata" jsonb DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb;
